796
00:42:28,400 --> 00:42:31,800
So here is a little
bit of background

797
00:42:31,800 --> 00:42:35,900
on the relevant
literature in this space.

798
00:42:35,900 --> 00:42:37,100
The rise of early reasoning.

799
00:42:37,100 --> 00:42:40,800
How early can we introduce
explicit reasoning the way

800
00:42:40,800 --> 00:42:42,920
we have in RLP?

801
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:45,920
And so there are three
papers, at least at the time

802
00:42:45,920 --> 00:42:47,820
our paper came out
in this space--

803
00:42:47,820 --> 00:42:50,860
Quiet-STaR reinforcement
pre-training,

804
00:42:50,860 --> 00:42:54,800
which is called RPT,
and reinforcement

805
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:59,880
learning on pre-training
data, which is called RLPT.

806
00:42:59,880 --> 00:43:02,400
And then our method
is called RLP.

807
00:43:02,400 --> 00:43:05,680
So here is a
qualitative comparison

808
00:43:05,680 --> 00:43:11,160
between our technique,
RLP, and RPT and RLP.

809
00:43:11,160 --> 00:43:12,990
So the source of reward.

810
00:43:12,990 --> 00:43:15,970
So in next token prediction,
you have no reward.

811
00:43:15,970 --> 00:43:20,830
Whereas in RPT and in RLPT,
you have an external verifier.

812
00:43:20,830 --> 00:43:25,270
You will need different model
to calculate the rewards.

813
00:43:25,270 --> 00:43:30,090
Whereas RLP is verifier-free
and it's intrinsic reward.

814
00:43:30,090 --> 00:43:33,090
The granularity of
the reward, it's

815
00:43:33,090 --> 00:43:35,890
sparse and binary
for RPT and RLPT

816
00:43:35,890 --> 00:43:39,430
because they use
RLVR style rewards.

817
00:43:39,430 --> 00:43:43,530
Whereas for RLP, as I
showed, it's a dense reward.

818
00:43:43,530 --> 00:43:47,610
And finally, reasoning
emergence is explicit and weak

819
00:43:47,610 --> 00:43:51,010
in case of RPT and RLPT,
but it's explicit and strong

820
00:43:51,010 --> 00:43:51,550
for RLP.

821
00:43:51,550 --> 00:43:54,090

822
00:43:54,090 --> 00:43:56,530
And here is a
quantitative comparison

823
00:43:56,530 --> 00:43:58,450
with the RPT technique.

824
00:43:58,450 --> 00:44:04,290
So we have used a setting that
is similar to the RPT paper.

825
00:44:04,290 --> 00:44:10,580
We use the Qwen31.7B-Base model
and we use the OmniMath dataset.

826
00:44:10,580 --> 00:44:14,620
And we train using RPT
technique and RLP technique

827
00:44:14,620 --> 00:44:17,300
on 170 million tokens.

828
00:44:17,300 --> 00:44:21,020
And as you can see, RLP
is on average 4% better

829
00:44:21,020 --> 00:44:23,580
compared to the RPT technique.

830
00:44:23,580 --> 00:44:26,540
And the reason behind
this is that RPT actually

831
00:44:26,540 --> 00:44:29,320
uses an external filter.

832
00:44:29,320 --> 00:44:32,180
So it's using a
completely different model

833
00:44:32,180 --> 00:44:35,180
to first go through
the pre-training data

834
00:44:35,180 --> 00:44:40,620
and select the tokens on which
this RPT reward can be applied.

835
00:44:40,620 --> 00:44:42,200
We do no such selection.

836
00:44:42,200 --> 00:44:47,380
You can apply RLT reward on
any token in your document.

837
00:44:47,380 --> 00:44:50,400
And RPT uses a
sparse binary reward.

838
00:44:50,400 --> 00:44:53,700
It's just a yes or no, 0 or 1.

839
00:44:53,700 --> 00:44:56,240
And reinforcing that
only select tokens

840
00:44:56,240 --> 00:44:58,780
and it ignores the
reasoning steps itself.

841
00:44:58,780 --> 00:45:03,420
Whereas in RLP, we apply
this dense per token reward

842
00:45:03,420 --> 00:45:06,380
based on information
gain, as I showed earlier.

843
00:45:06,380 --> 00:45:08,820
And that captures the
full reasoning signal

844
00:45:08,820 --> 00:45:12,780
because we are taking the
reasoning trace into account

845
00:45:12,780 --> 00:45:15,220
when we are
calculating the reward,

846
00:45:15,220 --> 00:45:17,660
and that we believe
is the reason why

847
00:45:17,660 --> 00:45:19,400
we get better results.

848
00:45:19,400 --> 00:45:22,180

849
00:45:22,180 --> 00:45:24,900
So the key ablations
and insights

850
00:45:24,900 --> 00:45:28,460
that we discussed
for RLP is that first

851
00:45:28,460 --> 00:45:32,440
is that we enable
thinking for itself,

852
00:45:32,440 --> 00:45:34,780
exploring and thinking for
itself during pre-training

853
00:45:34,780 --> 00:45:35,280
itself.

854
00:45:35,280 --> 00:45:38,220
So you get an
incentive or a reward

855
00:45:38,220 --> 00:45:40,240
for exploring and thinking.

856
00:45:40,240 --> 00:45:43,700
So there's info gain reward
on intermediate thoughts.

857
00:45:43,700 --> 00:45:49,660
And that outperforms simple
next-token prediction.

858
00:45:49,660 --> 00:45:53,440
The reward in RLP is
dense and not sparse,

859
00:45:53,440 --> 00:45:55,860
and it can be applied
at any position

860
00:45:55,860 --> 00:45:58,620
or at all positions
