1011
00:53:37,060 --> 00:53:50,660

1012
00:53:50,660 --> 00:53:51,160
Hello.

1013
00:53:51,160 --> 00:53:52,300
Thank you for the talk.

1014
00:53:52,300 --> 00:53:54,800
Could you speak a
little more on how

1015
00:53:54,800 --> 00:53:59,180
you quantify quality of data
in say, mathematical context?

1016
00:53:59,180 --> 00:54:01,120
That's quite clear, but
you also spoke a lot

1017
00:54:01,120 --> 00:54:05,120
about using a web crawler
or other more general bodies

1018
00:54:05,120 --> 00:54:06,080
of data?

1019
00:54:06,080 --> 00:54:08,880
And how could you possibly
go quantifying quality

1020
00:54:08,880 --> 00:54:10,400
in that context?

1021
00:54:10,400 --> 00:54:10,960
Right.

1022
00:54:10,960 --> 00:54:14,480
So there are many
approaches here.

1023
00:54:14,480 --> 00:54:19,740
The most popular being fine
web EDU-based classification.

1024
00:54:19,740 --> 00:54:25,880
So Hugging Face released this
where they've built classifiers

1025
00:54:25,880 --> 00:54:30,360
to tell how educational is
this content, given a web crawl

1026
00:54:30,360 --> 00:54:34,760
document, it scores it
on a scale of 1 to 5.

1027
00:54:34,760 --> 00:54:40,200
So even at NVIDIA, we
have adapted that scaling.

1028
00:54:40,200 --> 00:54:41,180
So that's one way.

1029
00:54:41,180 --> 00:54:45,520
There's also essential
web that also did

1030
00:54:45,520 --> 00:54:50,880
more types of classifications
in terms of not just

1031
00:54:50,880 --> 00:54:55,660
educational quality or
educational score, but domains,

1032
00:54:55,660 --> 00:54:58,040
whether it belongs
to science or math.

1033
00:54:58,040 --> 00:55:00,810
And also even within
education, whether it's

1034
00:55:00,810 --> 00:55:03,930
like intermediate or high
college level education

1035
00:55:03,930 --> 00:55:05,070
and so on and so forth.

1036
00:55:05,070 --> 00:55:09,590
So it depends on yeah, what
do you want to extract?

1037
00:55:09,590 --> 00:55:11,930
And you can build a classifier--

1038
00:55:11,930 --> 00:55:15,110
LLM-based classification
on rubric for that.

1039
00:55:15,110 --> 00:55:17,950
And you can classify
your documents that way.

1040
00:55:17,950 --> 00:55:20,830
But fine web EDU is
the most popular one.

1041
00:55:20,830 --> 00:55:25,450
And that's at least basic one
that is needed in some sense.

1042
00:55:25,450 --> 00:55:30,410

