1047
00:55:39,470 --> 00:55:40,550
Do you do it by--

1048
00:55:40,550 --> 00:55:42,270
I'm assuming you do it on
the highest quality data,

1049
00:55:42,270 --> 00:55:43,645
but do you choose
specific tokens

1050
00:55:43,645 --> 00:55:46,450
or just uniformly
across that data set?

1051
00:55:46,450 --> 00:55:47,830
That's a good question.

1052
00:55:47,830 --> 00:55:52,010
So theoretically,
RLP can be applied

1053
00:55:52,010 --> 00:55:55,090
on any token in a document.

1054
00:55:55,090 --> 00:55:57,130
In practice, when we
run the experiments,

1055
00:55:57,130 --> 00:56:00,480
we take a document, we just
randomly choose a token.

1056
00:56:00,480 --> 00:56:05,340
We don't really select it
using some fancy techniques

1057
00:56:05,340 --> 00:56:07,460
based on entropy and so on.

1058
00:56:07,460 --> 00:56:12,580
So we randomly select a token,
we apply our RLP technique

1059
00:56:12,580 --> 00:56:13,200
on it.

1060
00:56:13,200 --> 00:56:16,460
We backprop the reward, and
then we throw away that document

1061
00:56:16,460 --> 00:56:18,920
and we just get a new document.

1062
00:56:18,920 --> 00:56:19,420
Yeah.

1063
00:56:19,420 --> 00:56:20,040
So that's how.

1064
00:56:20,040 --> 00:56:22,420
And also to correct
you, we are actually

1065
00:56:22,420 --> 00:56:25,600
